Fix be-csharp's regex code sets: reach U+10FFFF, negate and merge right, and keep `\d` and `\w` whole.
Upstream: Temper branch fix-csharp-generic-names (8c44b571), not yet merged.

`CodeSetUniverse` ended at U+10FFFF exclusive, so a negated set
reaching U+10FFFF threw in `IntRangeSet.Negate`; `Negate` filled a
local list, missed the first range at the universe's start, and
appended the last gap only to trim it off; `Merge` wrote back only
merged ranges; and `Digit` and `Word` ranges dropped `9`, `Z`, and
`z`. As Kotlin's branch fixes them.

